WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.659
Hi it's me Michelle from Lab Muffin
Beauty science and today I'm going to be

00:00:03.659 --> 00:00:08.400
reviewing some products from Krave
Beauty. Krave Beauty is a new brand

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.330
launched by Korean skincare YouTuber
Liah Yoo who kindly sent me these

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:16.650
products to review. They don't usually
ship to Australia yet so I'm really

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:19.590
grateful that she sent them to me so
that I could actually get my hands on

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:24.619
them and try them out really early. So
far there are two products available:

00:00:24.619 --> 00:00:35.520
Kale-lalu-yAHA and the Matcha Hemp
Hydrating Cleanser. Krave Beauty is built

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.899
around the idea of simplicity: that the
basics of skincare should be basic, and

00:00:39.899 --> 00:00:43.980
skincare should respect your skin. And
they've definitely delivered with

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:51.690
their first two products. Krave Beauty is also
vegan, cruelty-free, alcohol-free, dye-free,

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:57.780
fragrance-free and essential oil-free.
Firstly: packaging. I personally find

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.859
packaging really important and I like
things to look nice on my shelf and

00:01:01.859 --> 00:01:06.420
Krave Beauty does look really good.
There's lots of natural colors with the

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.820
packaging.
There's even really nice natural colors

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:13.200
with the paper packaging on the outside
as well. I'm almost afraid to throw it

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.650
out because it's so pretty.
There's a photo of the star ingredient

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:21.090
on top for both. I really like that it's
got the instructions on the back which i

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:25.530
think is really important because if you
chuck out the paper packaging you're

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:31.079
just left with this. So tells you how to
use it, how often to use it, really nice

00:01:31.079 --> 00:01:35.850
coding as well - so it shows you morning
and night - so it's got like a little sun

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:43.680
and a moon... every single day... applying to
wet skin... Unfortunately Krave Beauty only

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:47.880
ships to the US and South Korea for
now, but they do have worldwide shipping

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:53.549
in the works.

00:01:53.549 --> 00:01:58.479
Kale-lalu-yAHA. Kale-lalu-yAHA is the first
of the supplement series.

00:01:58.479 --> 00:02:05.799
It's got 5.25% glycolic acid at a pH of
3.5 to 4 so it's weaker than most

00:02:05.799 --> 00:02:10.479
exfoliants you'll find, but it's not so
low that the glycolic acid is like a

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:16.000
vanity ingredient that does nothing, The
glycolic acid is in a base of soothing

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.650
and hydrating aloe water and butylene
glycol. It's also got lots of

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:24.280
antioxidants in it which are great for
potentially reducing free radical damage

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:30.700
So it's got kale, spinach and parsley
extracts. It's also got lots of hydrating

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:34.299
and soothing ingredients which I think
is really really good. So it's got

00:02:34.299 --> 00:02:40.810
hyaluronic acid, panthenol, which is also
called vitamin b5, allantoin. Allantoin is

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:46.060
particularly good for calming down
irritation, so if this very gentle

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:50.860
exfoliator does actually cause any
irritation it won't be as much of an

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:55.450
issue, because you've got these anti
irritants in there. This product is

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:59.829
really gentle and I think Kale-lalu-yAHA
is really really good for beginners who

00:02:59.829 --> 00:03:05.049
are just starting to use an alpha
hydroxy acid. It's really good for

00:03:05.049 --> 00:03:09.880
flattening out texture, dealing with
congestion, clogged pores, and give you

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:15.310
that glowy look. It's recommended that
you use this two to three times a week

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:21.640
but in reality, if your skin is quite
used to alpha hydroxy exfoliants, you can

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:26.350
probably just use it every night. I've
been using it every night. The most

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:31.780
similar product that I have in my stash
to Kale-lalu-yAHA is Pixi Glow Tonic. Pixi

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:37.600
Glow Tonic has 5% glycolic acid at pH 4
to 5, and the lower the pH the more

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:43.920
active the acid is. So Kale-lalu-yAHA is a
little bit stronger than Glow Tonic.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:49.060
Glow Tonic also has aloe vera as the
base as well, just like Kale-lalu-yAHA. It's

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:52.569
also got a few different extracts like
witch hazel and horse chestnut and

00:03:52.569 --> 00:03:58.780
they're both above 5%. And it's also got
a tiny bit of ginseng extract. The big

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:02.440
difference between the two in my
opinion is probably the fact that Pixi

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:06.720
Glow Tonic is fragranced and it's not
a particularly weak fragrance, it's sort

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:11.880
of moderate but it can bother some
people. Kale-lalu-yAHA is actually cheaper than

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:18.330
Glow Tonic - it's $25 for 200 mL versus
$15 for 100 mL. And this is in US

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:22.800
dollars, so this is how much it would be
if you bought it in America. In Australia

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:27.660
Glow Tonic is actually a bit more
expensive, so Kale-lalu-yAHA is an even

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:32.310
better bargain. I personally find that
Glow Tonic is nice but my skin loves

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:37.260
exfoliation, so I prefer a stronger
product. Kale-lalu-yAHA has also got more

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:42.210
humectants, and it's a bit more hydrating
on my dehydration prone skin. And it's

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:46.320
light and gentle enough that I can use
it daily. I've been using Kale-lalu-yAHA on

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:50.520
my face right after cleansing. It's
recommended that you use it on a cotton

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:55.260
pad, so you pour a little bit out and
then swipe it over your face. But wasting

00:04:55.260 --> 00:05:00.150
product hurts my soul a little bit, so I
use it without the cotton pad and I just

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:04.590
pour it on my face... pour it on my face. I
pour it on my hand and then I pat it on.

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:08.070
So I guess the palms of my hands are
probably going to be really nice and

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:13.800
glowing soon. I find it really nice to
have Kale-lalu-yAHA as an option in my stash.

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:18.780
There's not that many products like this
on the market. It's perfect for hydrating

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:23.160
skin and giving you gentle low-key
exfoliation without worrying about

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:26.940
stressing out your skin too much,
especially if it's already irritated

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:33.660
from other ingredients like retinol.
Make sure when you're using any alpha

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:38.580
hydroxy acid product you use sunscreen
as well. Alpha hydroxy acids can cause

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:43.110
photosensitivity for a week after you
use it. It doesn't really matter whether

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:46.680
you use alpha hydroxy acids in the
morning or night since the

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:50.270
photosensitivity
increases for so long afterwards anyway,

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:55.139
but I personally prefer using it at
night. If you haven't used an alpha

00:05:55.139 --> 00:05:59.550
hydroxy acid product before you might
get a bit of purging, but the soothing

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:03.389
ingredients should reduce the chances of
that. And if you want to find out more

00:06:03.389 --> 00:06:07.380
about purging I've got a whole video
about it and how to tell if your skin is

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:17.790
purging or just breaking out.
So overall, Kale-lalu-yAHA: love it. The

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:22.889
Matcha Hemp Hydrating Cleanser. This is
the first of the Core Series and it's a

00:06:22.889 --> 00:06:29.910
very gentle cleanser. It's $16 for 120
mL. It contains a whopping 40% matcha.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:34.199
Now if you look up studies on putting
matcha on your skin you won't actually

00:06:34.199 --> 00:06:38.550
find any studies because matcha is not
really the word they use in the

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:43.800
literature. You can find green tea
studies though, so matcha is actually a

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:48.750
form of green tea which has even more
antioxidants than normal. Green tea

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:52.520
contains chemicals called polyphenols
that can act as antioxidants.

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:57.599
Antioxidants are substances that can
soak up damage from free radicals. Free

00:06:57.599 --> 00:07:02.220
radicals are really reactive species
that have an unpaired electron. Free

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:06.300
radicals form from all sorts of things:
so environmental stressors like UV light

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:11.280
and pollution, and smoking if you're a
smoker. They can also form from just

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:15.240
normal biological processes. So free
radicals are important chemical

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:19.830
messengers in your body, but if they're
in the wrong place, because they're so

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:24.270
reactive, they can attack other things
inside your body, so things like cell

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:29.520
membranes, lipids, DNA. This free
radical damage which is also sometimes

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:34.740
called oxidative stress can build up and
then it leads to things like skin aging.

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:41.370
The key antioxidant polyphenol in green
tea is called epigallocatechin-3

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:47.070
gallate or EGCG.
It has 25 to 100 times as much

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:51.900
antioxidant ability as things like
vitamin C and E. Green tea also has a

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:55.890
bunch of other polyphenols which are
really antioxidant as well, and these are

00:07:55.890 --> 00:08:02.840
going to be really difficult for me to
say: epicatechin, epicatechin-3-gallate and

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:09.180
epigallocatechin. The way Krave Beauty
describes why they put matcha in this

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:12.600
product is that they thought it it'd be
awesome to splash matcha on your face

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:17.940
every day and I totally agree. This
cleanser has a pH of 5 to 6 which is

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:22.410
really good for skin. So cleansers
contain ingredients called surfactants

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:26.070
which is what does the cleansing. The
problem with surfactants is that they

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:30.420
can disturb your skin, so as well as
removing the lipids from your skin which

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:35.190
your skin needs, it can also bind to
proteins in your skin and change their

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:39.780
structure, which makes your skin barrier
more leaky, and this also makes them more

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:44.820
vulnerable to pH changes. High ph
cleansers are really bad for your skin

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:49.200
because they can change your skin pH for
extended amounts of time. The reason this

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:52.980
is bad for skin is that it tends to
interfere with the normal biological

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:58.290
processes in your skin that help it grow
and repair and exfoliate itself. All of

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:03.150
these biological processes tend to be pH
dependent. It's also got other nice

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:07.050
ingredients in it like hemp seed oil,
sweet almond oil and oat extract, which

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:11.010
is really soothing for your skin. Another
ingredient in this cleanser which I

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:15.630
think deserves a bit of cred is methyl
gluceth-10. It's not a really well known

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:18.930
ingredient probably because its name is
so uncatchy

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:23.790
but it's ingredient number 5 and it's
been in a few products that I've been

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:27.420
really liking lately.
Matcha Hemp Cleanser uses gentle

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:32.310
surfactants: so it's got coco-betaine which
is a zwitterionic surfactant, and non-

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:37.230
ionic surfactants like coco-glucoside
and decyl glucoside. It's also got soap

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:42.330
bark extract which contains more non-
ionic surfactants. I'm obsessed with

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:46.950
gentle surfactants in my cleansers
because of my dehydration prone skin. My

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:51.360
skin gets really sensitive when I use
too many harsh surfactants - they make my

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:55.440
skin really tight and itchy and
uncomfortable and it makes it a little

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:58.290
bit bumpy and it makes my pores look
even bigger

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:04.500
so gentle cleansing is probably my
number one skincare need. Another thing I

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:08.400
really like about this cleanser is that
it has a metric buttload of glycerin in

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:13.890
it - it's the third ingredient. Glycerin is
probably my favorite boring skincare

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:18.450
ingredient. It's a cheap humectant which
is really good at attracting and holding

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:22.800
onto water, and it's naturally already in
your skin. Glycerin seems to have more

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:27.990
special properties than fancy humectants
like hyaluronic acid - it can actually get

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:32.310
into the stratum corneum and stay there
for ages, so it's really really good for

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:38.190
dehydrated skin. The cleanser itself is a
clear slightly greenish brown gel and it

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:42.690
lathers up a little bit. It spreads
really really well on your skin so you

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:46.500
actually don't need very much I keep
squeezing a little bit too much and then

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:51.510
I end up washing my face and my neck is
on my chest as well. It smells a little

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:56.640
bit chemically, probably because it's
fragrance free. I really like that this

00:10:56.640 --> 00:11:01.020
cleanser gets rid of extra oil on my
skin without stripping it. Afterwards my

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:05.610
skin still feels really plump and soft
and not tight or squeaky which usually

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:11.070
means that my skin is drying out. It's
not amazing at makeup removal but it's

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:15.630
OK at removing light makeup. I've been
using it by itself on days when I stay

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:19.890
at home and don't actually wear much on
my face and I've been using it after

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:24.180
cleansing oil on days when I do wear
lots of makeup. I've been using this

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:28.470
daily in the shower and I even tried it
in the morning over the sink once which

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:32.760
is a pretty big deal for me. I hate
washing my face over the sink my

00:11:32.760 --> 00:11:36.690
bathroom set up really badly so every
time I try to wash my face over the sink

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:41.100
I end up bumping my head into the vanity,
I use tons of water to try to get the

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:45.030
cleanser off, it splashes everywhere, it
goes all the way all over the mirror and

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:47.970
there's little water drops on it
afterwards, and then it dries and

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:51.660
you have those little water marks and it
really really annoys me. And then when I

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:55.620
try to wipe off the water marks I leave
lint all over the mirror, and it's just

00:11:55.620 --> 00:12:02.190
impossible to get clean. So I hate hate
hate sink washing but I tried it over

00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:09.330
the sink. It doesn't work - well it works,
but nothing works for me over the sink

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:13.139
so unfortunately I wish I could
this cleanser convinced me to start

00:12:13.139 --> 00:12:18.329
washing my face over the sink, but no, it
seems like nothing is going to ever do

00:12:18.329 --> 00:12:23.479
that.

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:28.470
Overall I'm really really impressed with
these products. They're really gentle and

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:33.000
soothing and they slot in so easily
into my routine. I'm not really surprised

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:35.880
by how good they are because Liah's got
similar skin to mine:

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:40.800
she's got oily dehydrated and slightly
sensitive skin as well, plus she's been

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:44.459
reviewing beauty products for ages and
she worked at one of the biggest

00:12:44.459 --> 00:12:48.570
manufacturers of beauty products in
Korea so she's had tons of experience

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:52.350
with products, and she knows what works
well for her, and what works well for me

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:57.209
apparently. These are fantastic for
dehydrated skin. I'm really looking

00:12:57.209 --> 00:13:00.420
forward to seeing what Krave Beauty
comes out with next. I've seen that

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:04.470
Liah's been talking about sunscreen on
her Instagram and I know she's a big fan

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:08.640
of my favorite filters the Tinosorbs
S and M so I can't wait to see those

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:12.750
products. Thanks so much for watching my
review. If you like my videos you can

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:16.950
subscribe to my channel. If you have any
requests for videos please let me know!

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:21.240
You can also follow me on Instagram and
Facebook and of course I also have tons

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:31.850
of beauty science on my blog. See you
next time for more beauty science talk!

